{"name":"Greywacke","hex":"#aaccbb","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"greywacke","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A hard dark sandstone with poorly sorted angular grains of quartz, feldspar, and small rock fragments in a compact, clay-fine matrix."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/greywacke"}],"entries":[{"title":"Greywacke","blocks":[{"text":"Greywacke or graywacke is a variety of sandstone generally characterized by its hardness, dark color, and poorly sorted angular grains of quartz, feldspar, and small rock fragments or sand-size lithic fragments set in a compact, clay-fine matrix. It is a texturally immature sedimentary rock generally found in Paleozoic strata. The larger grains can be sand- to gravel-sized, and matrix materials generally constitute more than 15 percent of the rock by volume."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/Greywacke-f-and-l.jpg/330px-Greywacke-f-and-l.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Greywacke","wikidata":"Q917545"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fb/Menkaura_Bust_Closeup.jpg/330px-Menkaura_Bust_Closeup.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fb/Menkaura_Bust_Closeup.jpg/330px-Menkaura_Bust_Closeup.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Closeup of Pharaoh Menkaure's greywacke statue, 25th century BCE, from the Egyptian Museum in Cairo","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMenkaura_Bust_Closeup.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Grauwacke_AC_Rathaus.jpg/250px-Grauwacke_AC_Rathaus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Grauwacke_AC_Rathaus.jpg/500px-Grauwacke_